comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T00:18:03.112Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented and measured on fix/recovery-replays-invocation. exportedDeclarationClosure in scripts/release/package-distribution.mjs walks every exported types entry (11 unique) through relative from and import() specifiers, and reaches 473 of the 685 dist declarations. The staging loop skips any dist .d.ts outside that closure, and the checkout keeps every file. Gate receipts on the current build: base profile distribution_size 19,759,014 <= 20,000,000 with 1,589 <= 1,800 files (was 20,025,149 and 1,801). The Sentry-injected profile with --simulate-injection gives 20,037,538 <= 20,298,752 across 778 injected files. Headroom is now 240,986 B and 211 files, with ceilings unchanged. Proof: node scripts/smoke-npx-from-pack.mjs passed locally ('npx and bunx packed package smoke passed (2026.11.6, packages=9)'). Its strict consumer now imports all 12 exported types specifiers. Negative control: on an installed copy of the pruned tarball the same strict consumer compiles with exit 0. After removing the reachable dist/core/checkpoint/mutation-checkpoint.d.ts it fails with TS7016 from dist/sdk/runtime-primitives.d.ts, exit 2. Unit specs cover the closure (cycle, null export target, string targets, bare and .json specifiers, unpacked reference, unsupported specifier) and a real packDistribution fixture. In that fixture an unreachable dist declaration is dropped, while reachable and non-dist declarations ship. Targeted coverage of both scripts reports no uncovered branches or statements."
  "2026-11-07T00:55:24.703Z","harness:claude-code","Correction found by the full suite, which Codex round 15 missed: the exports-map premise holds only when the manifest declares exports. tests/integration/registry-acceptance-workflow.spec.ts packs a reviewed-controls fixture whose manifest has no exports or types, and the first version pruned its required dist/sdk/index.d.ts (required_path_missing). Without an exports map every subpath stays deep-importable, so stageSourceFiles now prunes only when manifest.exports is defined. The fixture pack spec re-packs without exports and asserts that every declaration ships. docs/RELEASING.md states the rule. pm-cli's own manifest declares exports, so the measured savings are unchanged (gate: 19,760,781 B / 1,589 files)."
